        "username": "DouglasOsborn",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/douglasosborn/{size}/6711_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-09-20T19:42:05.911Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Recently started transferring the characters I had created from scratch paper onto the Hero Sheet PDF.  I noticed that there are only six slots each for Powers and Qualities.  This got me wondering if the most Powers or Qualities one could have is six apiece?  Realizing that one can only have (at most) twelve Powers and Qualities, but I haven’t found anything in the character creation rules that established that these twelve must be split six and six.  Is this just a limitation of the space on the Hero Sheet, or is there actual guidance on how many of each is allowed?  Without any official limitation, it would be possible to get 7 (or even 8) of either Powers or Qualities.<br>\nFor those wondering, my totals were derived as follows:<br>\nBackground yields 2 Qualities (3 in the case of Struggling and Medical);<br>\nPower Source yields 2 or 3 Powers depending on your Background dice (Plus, seven Power Sources can grant 1 additional Power or quality;<br>\nArchetype yields 2 or 3 Powers or Qualities depending on your Power Source dice;<br>\nBackground Concept counts as a Quality;<br>\nAnd finally, Retcon allows the addition of 1 Power or Quality.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2024-09-20T19:42:05.911Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
