        "id": 260906,
        "name": "FrivYeti",
        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-09-20T19:56:05.804Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Nope, it’s just a sheet limitation based on the most common outcomes in the game. There’s no actual rule to how many of each you’re allowed to have.</p>\n<p>You can actually get <em>more</em> power or quality dice than that. The highest number of power or quality dice is nine.</p>\n<p>For powers, that’s three granted from your power source, then one granted by the Supernatural, Alien, or Multiverse power source, then three more from your Archetype, then one from the Robot/Cyborg Archetype, then one from your retcon)</p>\n<p>For qualities, it’s three granted from the Medical or Struggling background, then one granted from the Training, Mystical, Genius, or Unknown power source, then three from the Shadow or Close Quarters Combatant Archetypes, then your RP quality from the Personality step, then one more from retcon.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2024-09-20T19:56:05.804Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 5,
